---
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const LAST_UPDATED = "September 28, 2026";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <SEO
      title="Privacy Policy — cntxt"
      description="cntxt's privacy policy: what data the browser extension collects, why, and how to request deletion."
      path="/privacy"
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <article class="policy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

        <p>
          cntxt is a browser extension that turns each browser window into a
          named "Project", and its tab groups into "Groups": saved lists of
          tabs you can close and restore later. This policy explains what
          data the extension collects, why, and how you can have it removed.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Project and Group data.</strong> The name, color, icon, and
            tab list (page title and URL — not page content) of each Project
            and Group you create. This is stored on your device via the
            browser's built-in storage. Tab titles and URLs are, by their
            nature, a record of the sites you've visited while a tab belonged
            to a Project or Group.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Account email.</strong> If you choose to sign in (via an
            emailed one-time code), we store your email address to identify
            your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Authentication tokens.</strong> Session tokens issued by our
            authentication provider (Supabase) so you stay signed in.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not read the content of the pages in your tabs, your browsing
          history outside of saved Projects and Groups, your keystrokes, clicks, or
          mouse activity, and we do not collect health, financial, or location
          data.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          Project and Group data, your account email, and authentication tokens exist
          for one purpose: to let you save, close, and restore a window's tabs
          — and, only if you sign in, to sync that same data across your
          devices. Nothing here is used for advertising, profiling, or any
          purpose unrelated to that.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
        <p>
          If you never sign in, everything stays local to your browser via
          chrome.storage and never leaves your device. If you sign in,
          Project and Group data, your email, and session tokens are also stored on
          <a href="https://supabase.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Supabase</a
          >, the backend we use for sync — under our account, not shared or
          resold to any other party.
        </p>

        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>
          Upgrading to a paid plan opens a checkout page hosted by <a
            href="https://www.creem.io"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Creem</a
          >, our payment processor. cntxt never sees or stores your card
          details — Creem handles the transaction and tells us only that a
          given account has an active subscription.
        </p>

        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We don't sell or transfer your data to third parties.</li>
          <li>
            We don't use your data for anything outside the single purpose
            described above.
          </li>
          <li>
            We don't use your data to determine creditworthiness or for
            lending purposes.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can delete individual Projects and Groups at any time from the
          extension. To delete your account and all associated data, or to
          ask what data we hold about you, email <a
            href="mailto:privacy@cntxt.work">privacy@cntxt.work</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top of this
          page.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:privacy@cntxt.work"
            >privacy@cntxt.work</a
          >.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  a {
    color: var(--accent-alt1);
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy {
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .policy h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    color: var(--surface-txt-hint);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--surface-txt);
  }
</style>
